{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q18378715","formula":"C₂₂H₃₅NO₃","hill":"C22H35NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":22.0,"H":35.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"N-arachidonoylglycine"},"descriptions":{"en":"N-Arachidonylglycine (NAGly) is a carboxylic metabolite of the endocannabinoid anandamide (AEA). Since it was first synthesized in 1996, NAGly has been a primary focus of the relatively contemporary field of lipidomics due to its wide range of signaling targets in the brain, the immune system and throughout various other bodily systems. In combination with 2‐arachidonoyl glycerol (2‐AG), NAGly has enabled the identification of a family of lipids often referred to as endocannabinoids."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":5283389,"mass":361.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCC/C=C\\C/C=C\\C/C=C\\C/C=C\\CCCC(=O)NCC(=O)O","inchikey":"YLEARPUNMCCKMP-DOFZRALJSA-N","iupac":"2-[[(5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-icosa-5,8,11,14-tetraenoyl]amino]acetic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"5283389","atoms":61,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-5.242,"y":0.663,"z":3.934,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.172,"y":-0.497,"z":3.611,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.245,"y":-0.832,"z":2.118,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.306,"y":-1.958,"z":1.664,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.807,"y":-1.658,"z":1.709,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.406,"y":-0.51,"z":0.826,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.866,"y":-0.578,"z":-0.403,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.564,"y":-1.81,"z":-1.209,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.309,"y":-1.784,"z":-2.513,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.791,"y":-1.782,"z":-3.754,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.341,"y":-1.846,"z":-4.141,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.827,"y":-0.496,"z":-4.55,"el":"C"},{"x":0.195,"y":0.195,"z":-4.018,"el":"C"},{"x":1.094,"y":-0.203,"z":-2.883,"el":"C"},{"x":0.933,"y":0.73,"z":-1.717,"el":"C"},{"x":1.826,"y":1.621,"z":-1.254,"el":"C"},{"x":3.178,"y":1.928,"z":-1.835,"el":"C"},{"x":4.